      "slug": "herringbone-htr",
      "term": "Herringbone half treble",
      "definition": "A variation on the half treble crochet: instead of drawing the loop through all three loops at once, the working yarn is pulled through the first loop only, then through the remaining two. This creates a diagonal stitch that mimics a herringbone weave."
    }
  ],
